cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DRAgNEt: Deep Research Agent Network for Etymology"
message: "If you use DRAgNEt Case Files, primary-scan proof plates, verified JSON citation ledgers, or claim-level evidence graphs in your research, please cite the individual Case File or this repository."
type: dataset
version: "3.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
authors:
  - family-names: "Callahan"
    given-names: "Joshua"
repository-code: "https://github.com/radbot44/dragnet-etymology"
url: "https://dragnet.tch.one"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  Open-access historical lexicography dataset and AI-authored working-paper archive
  coordinated by Joshua Callahan (DRAgNEt — Deep Research Agent Network for Etymology).
  Publishes machine-validated JSON citation ledgers (schema 3.0), structured claim-level
  evidence graphs and inferential DAGs (schema 1.0), precision-bounded antedating
  baselines, negative-evidence corpus bounds, verbatim diplomatic transcriptions,
  rejected OCR/misdate leads, and pre-1931 U.S. public-domain newspaper, periodical,
  and court-record scans verified against primary archival repositories, with
  cryptographic SHA-256 review provenance separating discovered, agent_verified,
  human_verified, and externally_recognized citations as well as unreviewed,
  agent_reviewed, independently_agent_reviewed, and human_reviewed claims.
keywords:
  - etymology
  - historical lexicography
  - antedating
  - American slang
  - archival verification
  - claim-level evidence
  - provenance graph
